title: Dealing with Toleration
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/portraits/lerroux.jpg
view-if: dealing_with_toleration_timer = 0 and psoe_toleration and chancellor_party == "Z"
on-arrival: dealing_with_toleration_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs
#subtitle: Despite not being in government, we can still provide support.

= Dealing with Toleration

We are currently acting as external support to the government of President [+ chancellor +]. How should we use our position?

- @break_toleration
- @urge_against_austerity
- @improve_relations
- @stay_course: Stay the course, for stability's sake.
- @easy_discard

@break_toleration
view-if: not constructive_vonc
title: End the toleration agreement with a vote of no confidence!

Are we sure about this? A vote of no confidence would trigger new elections, and potentially an increased vote-share for the extremist parties.

- @vonc: Yes, end this arrangement!
- @stay_course: No, we should stay the course.

@vonc
on-arrival: psoe_in_government = 0; psoe_toleration = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Chapaprieta"; chancellor_party = "I"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; psoe_toleration = 0; caballeristas_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 5; middle_psoe -= 6; rural_psoe -= 3; catholics_psoe -= 3; prietistas_dissent += 5; caballeristas_dissent -= 5; workers_ap += 6; middle_ap += 5; rural_pce += 3;

We have called for a vote of no confidence, and have brought down this government. President [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting President of the Council of Ministers.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@urge_against_austerity
title: Urge the coalition against austerity politics, and to increase social spending.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and chancellor_party == "PRR"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget <= 0 : This can only happen with a budget surplus. ?] [? if chancellor_party != "PRR" : Austerity isn't something they would plan to do anyway. ?]
go-to: urge_success if prr_relation >= 40; urge_failure if prr_relation < 40

@urge_success
on-arrival: welfare += 1; budget -= 1; workers_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); dlr_relation -= 3; prr_relation -= 3; prietistas_dissent -= 5; caballeristas_dissent -= 5; besteiristas_dissent -= 5;

We have successfully urged the coalition parties to increase social spending! Unfortunately, the center-right parties increasingly see us as a nuisance, and might not wish to continue these negotiations.

@urge_failure
on-arrival: prr_relation -= 3; dlr_relation -= 3

Unfortunately, our negotiations have met with failure. The center-right parties increasingly see us as a nuisance, and might not wish to continue these negotiations.


@improve_relations
title: Improve relations with the parties of the coalition.
on-arrival: prr_relation += 5*(1-dissent) if in_republican_socialist_conjunction; prrs_relation += 4*(1-dissent); ar_relation += 4*(1-dissent); caballeristas_dissent += 5;

We have increased our level of contact and discussions with the main parties of the coalition.

Our attempts to reach out to the moderates are met with disdain by leftists within our party.


@stay_course

We will stay the course of toleration, for the sake of stability.
